  "step_2": "The individual in the verbal report states: 'Der Unterschied der beiden Summen ist so gering, dass ich lieber eine nur geringfügig größere Warscheinlichkeit habe überhaupt geld zu erhalten, als etwas mehr.' This translates to: 'The difference in the amounts is so small that I would rather have only a slightly higher probability of receiving any money than a slightly larger amount.' The individual acknowledges that the difference in outcomes (2500 vs. 2400) is negligible. They emphasize preferring a slightly higher probability of receiving any money (i.e., receiving something) over a slightly larger amount. The individual also mentions comparing the importance of receiving money versus the sum and has decided on receiving money. The deliberation centers on the value of the probability of obtaining any money, not the amount received. This aligns with focusing on the probability of a favorable outcome, treating the monetary difference as negligible.",
  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — that the outcomes are nearly identical and the probability of receiving money is slightly higher in Lottery B — is acknowledged by the individual. The individual explicitly states a preference for a slightly higher probability of receiving any money over a slightly larger amount, which matches the rule of the decision reason: 'The differences between the outcomes are negligible; the reason prefers the lottery with the higher probability of obtaining a favorable outcome.' The justification in the verbal report directly reflects this rule. Therefore, the individual used the decision reason to make the decision.",
  "final_assessment_score": 100
